MASTER_CHARACTER=A big friendly brown bear baker with a chunky, heavy, round body, wide and stout: warm honey-brown fur, a round light-tan muzzle with a dark-brown nose, small round ears, and a big round belly. A white long-sleeved baker's shirt whose sleeves are pushed up a little: each white sleeve ends in a soft rolled cuff on the forearm, and a short band of honey-brown furry forearm shows between the cuff and the paw. A short red-and-white checked apron tied at the waist with a red waistband over the shirt, covering the front of the hips and ending just below the crotch. Wide brown trousers on short sturdy legs, the two trouser legs a little apart below the apron. Dark-brown wooden clogs. Dark chocolate-brown mitten paws, darker than the fur. No hat. Both paws are empty: no tools or props. The bear has no visible tail.
CHARACTER=A big friendly brown bear baker with a chunky, heavy, round body: warm honey-brown fur, a round light-tan muzzle with a dark-brown nose, small round ears, and a big round belly. A white baker's shirt whose sleeves are pushed up to the elbows in a thick soft white roll; below the roll the honey-brown furry forearms are bare down to the paws. A short red-and-white checked apron tied at the waist with a red waistband over the shirt, hanging over the front of the trousers to just below the crotch. Wide brown trousers on short sturdy legs. Dark-brown wooden clogs. Dark chocolate-brown mitten paws, darker than the fur. No hat, no tail. Both paws are empty: no tools or props.
PIECES=Row 1: head base (the round honey-brown bear head with its light-tan muzzle and dark-brown nose, plain fur forehead and eye areas), left ear, right ear (small round honey-brown ears with a light-tan inside). Row 2: torso (the white shirt over the big round belly, continuing up into a short honey-brown fur neck and ending at the top of the red apron waistband; both shoulders are rounded white shirt, and the shirt sides are painted down to the waist; no apron, waistband, trousers or legs on it), hips (the whole lower body as ONE piece: the red apron waistband, the red-and-white checked apron and the wide brown trousers behind it, painted whole from the top of the waistband down to both trouser hems, the two trouser legs a little apart with background between them below the crotch, each leg ending in a rounded open hem with nothing below it; no clogs on it). Row 3: four separate arm pieces, each painted upright: left upper arm, right upper arm (the white shirt sleeve from the shoulder down to its thick rolled cuff at the elbow, rounded at the top), left forearm, right forearm (the bare honey-brown furry forearm from the elbow down to the wrist, rounded at both ends); then left paw, right paw (dark chocolate-brown mitten paws, open and relaxed, rounded at the wrist). Row 4: left clog, right clog (the dark-brown wooden clogs, rounded at the top where the trouser hem covers them).
HANDS=relaxed (exactly the paw of image_1, open and relaxed); open (palm facing the viewer, all fingers spread wide, as in a wave); fist, palm side facing the viewer: the curled fingers and the thumb across them visible; point, the palm facing the viewer: index finger stretched straight down, the other fingers curled onto the palm with their tips visible; thumbs-up (fingers curled into a fist, thumb sticking straight out sideways, away from the body); grip (fingers curled loosely forward and the thumb pressed against the side of the first finger, as when pinching something thin).
POSES=Row 1: left clog, left clog on tiptoe, right clog, right clog on tiptoe (the dark-brown wooden clogs, each with its rounded top where the trouser hem covers it; on tiptoe the clog is seen from the front with its toe pointing down and its sole tilted towards the viewer, as when jumping, with its rounded top still at the top).
SLEEVE=the white shirt sleeve pushed up to the elbow plus the bare forearm: from the rounded white shoulder down to the thick soft white rolled cuff at the elbow halfway down, then the bare honey-brown furry forearm below the roll down to the wrist
PROPS=Left: a small white flag on a thin straight wooden stick: the stick is vertical, as long as the character's whole arm, and the plain white rectangular cloth hangs from the top third of the stick out to the right with two soft folds; nothing is drawn on the cloth. Right: a low wooden hurdle seen straight from the front: two short upright posts on small feet and one horizontal crossbar painted red and white, about as tall as the character's clogs and trousers up to the knee, and about as wide as the character's hips.
POINT=point, the palm facing the viewer: the inside of the paw toward us with its soft lighter palm pad, index finger stretched straight down, the other fingers curled onto the palm with their rounded tips visible, and the thumb sticking out sideways from the outer side, chunky dark chocolate-brown mitten paw like image_1
